content:
Help me define bounded contexts. Below I will provide domain information. 

#### Data:
These are the extracted objects and the subdomain grouping:
```json
{
  "domain objects": [
    {
      "name": "Pet Owner",
      "description": "Person who requests and pays for pet sitting services"
    },
    {
      "name": "Pet Care Request",
      "description": "Request describing how a pet should be cared for during a time period",
      "attributes": [
        "Pet",
        "Time Period",
        "Care Instructions"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Pet",
      "description": "Animal that requires care"
    },
    {
      "name": "Time Period",
      "description": "Span of time during which care is needed"
    },
    {
      "name": "Care Instructions",
      "description": "Details about feeding, walking, or medication needs"
    },
    {
      "name": "Pet Sitter",
      "description": "Person who performs the pet care visit"
    },
    {
      "name": "Update Log",
      "description": "Record of updates the sitter sends during a visit"
    },
    {
      "name": "Schedule Coordination",
      "description": "Coordination process for handling overlapping or shared schedules"
    },
    {
      "name": "Care Report",
      "description": "Summary of the pet’s activities and behavior after a visit"
    },
    {
      "name": "Coordinator",
      "description": "Person who manages bookings and sitter assignments"
    },
    {
      "name": "Booking",
      "description": "Confirmed arrangement between owner, sitter, and request"
    },
    {
      "name": "Payment",
      "description": "Transaction made by the owner to complete the booking"
    },
    {
      "name": "Reminder",
      "description": "Notification sent about an upcoming booking",
      "attributes": [
        "Booking"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```
```json
{
  "subdomains": {
    "Pet Care": {
      "objects": [
        "Pet Sitter",
        "Care Report",
        "Update Log",
        "Pet Care Request"
      ]
    },
    "Customer Requests": {
      "objects": [
        "Pet Owner",
        "Pet Care Request",
        "Pet",
        "Time Period",
        "Care Instructions",
        "Payment"
      ]
    },
    "Organisation": {
      "objects": [
        "Coordinator",
        "Pet Sitter",
        "Schedule Coordination",
        "Booking",
        "Pet Care Request"
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

#### Task:
- Assign the subdomains to bounded contexts. 
- Name the subdomain the bounded context might be derived from, it might also be multiple.
- Identify cases, where an object does not have a unified meaning across all bounded contexts and suggest a name change.
- Return the bounded contexts in json format. Here is an example for structuring the data:
```json
{
  "bounded contexts": {
    "...": {
      "derived from": "...",
      "objects": [
        "...",
        "..."
      ],
      "name changes": []
    },
    "...": {
      "derived from": "...",
      "objects": [
        "...",
        "...",
        "..."
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "... -> ..."
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

Here are the bounded contexts: 
```json
{
  "bounded contexts": {
    "Pet Care": {
      "derived from": "Pet Care Subdomain",
      "objects": [
        "Pet Sitter",
        "Care Report",
        "Update Log",
        "Pet Care Job"
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "Pet Care Request -> Pet Care Job"
      ]
    },
    "Customer Requests": {
      "derived from": "Customer Requests Subdomain",
      "objects": [
        "Pet Owner",
        "Pet Care Request",
        "Pet",
        "Time Period",
        "Care Instructions",
        "Payment"
      ],
      "name changes": []
    },
    "Organisation": {
      "derived from": "Organisation Subdomain",
      "objects": [
        "Coordinator",
        "Sitter Assignment",
        "Schedule Coordination",
        "Booking",
        "Pet Care Appointment"
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "Pet Sitter -> Sitter Assignment",
        "Pet Care Request -> Pet Care Appointment"
      ]
    }
  }
}
```
